1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,956
Gartner found that more than half of generative AI projects were abandoned after proof of concept.

2
00:00:05,956 --> 00:00:08,252
Rarely because the model was wrong.

3
00:00:08,252 --> 00:00:11,058
Usually because of everything built around it.

4
00:00:11,058 --> 00:00:12,028
Cost.

5
00:00:12,028 --> 00:00:13,086
Governance.

6
00:00:13,086 --> 00:00:14,591
Unclear value.

7
00:00:14,591 --> 00:00:18,775
And a lot of that gets rebuilt for every single application.

8
00:00:18,775 --> 00:00:25,267
In the last video, the idea was to build those AI capabilities once, and let applications connect to them.

9
00:00:25,267 --> 00:00:27,933
That is Ask-AI MCP Service.

10
00:00:27,933 --> 00:00:29,732
Here is it actually running.

11
00:00:29,732 --> 00:00:35,408
This is one application, a case management system, with three different kinds of user.

12
00:00:35,408 --> 00:00:39,094
Two people ask the same system about the same case.

13
00:00:39,094 --> 00:00:40,982
Should they get the same answer?

14
00:00:40,982 --> 00:00:44,770
Someone in day to day operations asks about a case.

15
00:00:44,770 --> 00:00:47,397
They get back what they need to act on.

16
00:00:47,397 --> 00:00:50,165
The dates, and what is still outstanding.

17
00:00:50,165 --> 00:00:54,298
Now the same case, asked by someone doing deeper review.

18
00:00:54,298 --> 00:00:58,035
Same system, same record, and the answer is different.

19
00:00:58,035 --> 00:00:59,387
The full file.

20
00:00:59,387 --> 00:01:02,640
Who is involved, where it sits, who is deciding.

21
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:06,747
The person's job changes the reasoning, not just what they are allowed to see.

22
00:01:06,747 --> 00:01:11,071
And for someone working with the data, a question in plain English.

23
00:01:11,071 --> 00:01:16,505
Ask-AI MCP Service writes the query, runs it, and returns the chart.

24
00:01:16,505 --> 00:01:18,698
You can see the SQL it generated.

25
00:01:18,698 --> 00:01:21,403
Nobody built that dashboard in advance.

26
00:01:21,403 --> 00:01:24,374
One shared service underneath all three.

27
00:01:24,374 --> 00:01:28,520
Each application still owns its own logic and its own data.

28
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:29,936
Try it yourself.

29
00:01:29,936 --> 00:01:36,058
The Ask-AI MCP Service demo is linked in the post, and I would like to know what you would want it to answer.

